BEFORE INSTALLING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] In RangeWater 1.0.1, create a fresh .rangewater backup outside the app.
[ ] Confirm the backup file is visible in Drive or another durable folder.
[ ] Do not uninstall until the backup is confirmed.

SIGNATURE NOTE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The field APK uses RangeWater's stable field-test certificate. Google Play installations
use Google's production app-signing certificate. Android will not install one signature
over the other. If the device currently has the Google Play build, use this field path:
backup -> uninstall Play build -> install field APK -> restore backup.

The exact Play-to-Play in-place schema migration must be verified later through Google
Play internal testing with versionCode 19. The automated Room suite has already migrated a
populated real schema-6 database to schema 7 without destructive fallback.

FIELD TEST — DATA AND MAP SURVIVAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] Install RangeWater 1.1.0 field APK.
[ ] Restore the fresh 1.0.1 backup when a cross-signature reinstall was required.
[ ] Confirm pastures, waters, assignments, gates, herds, movements, camera, and layer
    preferences survived or restored correctly.
[ ] Confirm ordinary water-coverage acreage still matches the accepted map.

FIELD TEST — GRAZING CIRCUITS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] Open Herds -> Manage Grazing Circuits -> Create Circuit.
[ ] Name it and select at least four mapped pastures.
[ ] Give one pasture two roles, including Stockpiled Winter Grazing.
[ ] Use explicit Up and Down controls to reorder the pastures; save.
[ ] Close RangeWater completely, reopen it, and confirm name, notes, order, and roles.
[ ] Assign an existing herd to the circuit; confirm its physical location did not change.
[ ] Open that herd and confirm circuit name, member count, and circuit position.
[ ] Focus the herd. Confirm every circuit pasture uses the herd color, current pasture is
    strongest, unrelated pastures dim, other herd badges hide, and relevant water/gates stay.
[ ] Clear Focus. Confirm the complete ranch and saved layer preferences return exactly.
[ ] Move the herd through the accepted movement workflow; confirm circuit membership stays.
[ ] Move it outside the circuit and confirm the outside-circuit warning appears.
[ ] Confirm an assigned circuit cannot be archived.
[ ] Confirm a pasture in a circuit cannot be deleted and the blocker names the circuit.

FIELD TEST — RECORDED REST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] Complete a movement out of a pasture.
[ ] Open that pasture and confirm "Recorded rest" uses the latest completed departure.
[ ] Confirm an occupied pasture says occupied instead of showing a running rest total.
[ ] Confirm a pasture with no qualifying departure says "No recorded departure."
[ ] Cold reopen and confirm the result is derived again from movement history.

FIELD TEST — FORAGE / STOCKPILE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] Open a pasture -> Forage.
[ ] Enter sample count and average height in inches.
[ ] Exercise each Ohio stand type and condition needed to verify the printed stick table.
[ ] Hand-check one calculation: max(height - residual, 0) x lb DM/acre/in x mapped acres.
[ ] Confirm low/high pounds per acre, mapped pounds, and tons match the hand calculation.
[ ] Confirm the mapped-acre limitation is visible before saving.
[ ] Save an observation and confirm the latest estimate appears on the pasture card.
[ ] For a Stockpiled Winter Grazing pasture, confirm the label says Latest stockpile estimate.
[ ] Edit the pasture boundary; confirm the old observation retains its acreage snapshot and
    a new observation uses the new mapped acreage.
[ ] Record one Other / Custom calibration and confirm its entered low/high range is used.

FIELD TEST — ARCHIVE SAFETY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
